{"analysis": "The debug output reveals that the model predicts token 93 ("~") after "Once upon a time", which is clearly wrong. The tokenization is confirmed correct. The model works for single-token inputs ("The" → reasonable predictions) but fails for multi-token inputs. This suggests a bug in the attention mechanism for positions > 0. The gen loop in dbg17 has a bug (lm initialized to 0 instead of the first token's logit), but the main program is correct. I need to test a batch-mode forward pass to see if the issue is with the sequential processing or the model itself.",
  "plan": "Write a debug program with a batch-mode forward pass that processes all tokens simultaneously for each layer, and compare predictions with the sequential approach. This will help determine if the issue is with the sequential KV cache or the model weights.",
